id: pmc-zj2w
title: "Extension surface has no --no-pending-release equivalent (Greptile issue 1, PR #174)"
description: "Greptile review on PR #174 (confidence 3/5): When pm changelog generate --all-release-tags --release-version-from-package runs in a never-tagged package, the extension passes the package version as pending but exposes no suppression flag and never forwards pendingRelease: false. So the extension keeps producing the fabricated dated heading that the standalone CLI now avoids. Two surfaces, same intent, divergent behaviour."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[3]: bug,greptile,pr-174
created_at: "2026-08-31T11:19:44.449Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-02T10:53:46.176Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-02T10:53:45.839Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-02T10:53:45.839Z"
author: pi-agent
resolution: "The cross-surface regression fixture explicitly requests empty sections on both the standalone CLI and SDK extension paths, so a synthetic untagged pending release remains observable after the real package version is tagged and the tracker has no post-tag completions."
expected_result: "CLI and extension emit byte-identical output with and without pending-release suppression on every repository release state, while both logical branches remain exercised by exact coverage."
actual_result: "After merging origin/main at tagged 2026.9.1, the focused test passes 1/1 and the full suite passes 544/544 with exact 100.00% line, branch, and function coverage."
comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-31T11:23:26.796Z",pi-agent,"Fixed: added --no-pending-release flag to extension changelog generate command and forwarded pendingRelease through resolveReleaseTagWindows. Equivalence test asserts CLI and extension produce byte-identical output with and without the flag. Revert-proof: test fails when the pendingRelease forwarding is removed."
  "2026-09-02T10:52:23.837Z",codex,"Duplicate/lineage check: this is the exact test introduced for pmc-zj2w. No new item is needed. After merging origin/main, v2026.9.1 contains every completed tracker item, so the synthetic 2099 pending window is valid but empty and filtered from visible output. The product path remains correct; the test must request include-empty on both CLI and extension surfaces to observe the window it is comparing."
  "2026-09-02T10:53:45.418Z",codex,"Verification after current-main merge: focused equivalence test passes 1/1 with include-empty on both surfaces. Full coverage then passes 544/544 with exact 100.00% lines, branches, and functions; docstring gate passes 184/184; production audit reports zero vulnerabilities; pack dry-run succeeds. The only later release:check failure was expected tracker/changelog drift because this item was temporarily reopened for the fix."
files[2]{path,scope,note}:
  src/extension.ts,project,Added --no-pending-release flag and forwarded pendingRelease
  test/extension.test.ts,project,Added --no-pending-release to flag contract list and byte-identical equivalence test
tests[1]{command,scope,note}:
  npx tsx --test test/extension.test.ts,project,CLI and extension produce byte-identical output with and without --no-pending-release
close_reason: Extension-equivalence coverage is now independent of whether current main has unreleased completed items.
body: ""
